1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:01,345
Welcome back!

2
00:00:01,345 --> 00:00:06,545
Invoices are great for treatment plans,
but sometimes you just need to get paid,

3
00:00:06,545 --> 00:00:07,065
quickly.

4
00:00:07,065 --> 00:00:11,875
In this lesson, we'll cover three
faster options: payment links, Text2Pay,

5
00:00:11,875 --> 00:00:12,915
and order forms.

6
00:00:13,767 --> 00:00:17,587
A payment link is a checkout
page for one or more products,

7
00:00:17,587 --> 00:00:19,206
with its own web address.

8
00:00:19,206 --> 00:00:22,702
You create it once, and share
it as often as you like.

9
00:00:22,702 --> 00:00:26,004
This whitening link has
already been paid 14 times.

10
00:00:26,856 --> 00:00:29,146
Let's make one for a check-up and clean.

11
00:00:29,146 --> 00:00:32,353
Click Create payment link,
name it, and add the product.

12
00:00:32,353 --> 00:00:36,304
Prices come straight from your
product list, so they're always right.

13
00:00:37,153 --> 00:00:39,331
Choose what the checkout asks for.

14
00:00:39,331 --> 00:00:43,238
Collecting a phone number is
handy for appointment reminders.

15
00:00:43,238 --> 00:00:47,914
You can also allow coupon codes, and
decide what happens after payment: a

16
00:00:47,914 --> 00:00:51,053
confirmation page, or a
page on your own website.

17
00:00:51,903 --> 00:00:54,057
Click Create link, and it's ready.

18
00:00:54,057 --> 00:00:57,920
Copy it into a text, an email,
a social post or your website.

19
00:00:57,920 --> 00:00:59,314
There's a QR code too.

20
00:00:59,314 --> 00:01:03,177
Print it at reception, and
patients can pay from their phone.

21
00:01:03,177 --> 00:01:06,028
When an offer ends, just
switch its link off.

22
00:01:06,879 --> 00:01:07,830
Next, Text2Pay.

23
00:01:07,830 --> 00:01:11,949
It's perfect for a one-off amount
for one person, like a deposit.

24
00:01:11,949 --> 00:01:14,167
You'll find it on the Invoices tab.

25
00:01:14,167 --> 00:01:19,237
It creates a quick invoice, and texts the
payment link straight to the patient's

26
00:01:19,237 --> 00:01:19,617
phone.

27
00:01:19,617 --> 00:01:24,117
It's ideal straight after a phone
call, when someone has just said yes.

28
00:01:24,966 --> 00:01:28,515
Pick the customer, Liam Patel,
and his number fills in.

29
00:01:28,515 --> 00:01:31,741
Choose the item: the implant
consultation deposit.

30
00:01:31,741 --> 00:01:35,290
The message on the right is
exactly what Liam will see.

31
00:01:35,290 --> 00:01:38,323
Click Send, and he can
pay in a couple of taps.

32
00:01:39,155 --> 00:01:43,412
Because Text2Pay creates an invoice,
you can track it here like any other.

33
00:01:43,412 --> 00:01:46,576
You can also send payment
requests from a conversation,

34
00:01:46,576 --> 00:01:48,704
while you're chatting with a patient.

35
00:01:49,554 --> 00:01:50,932
Finally, order forms.

36
00:01:50,932 --> 00:01:53,557
These live on your funnels and websites.

37
00:01:53,557 --> 00:01:57,626
You add an order form element
to a page in the funnel builder,

38
00:01:57,626 --> 00:01:59,529
which we covered in Module 7.

39
00:01:59,529 --> 00:02:02,154
Every purchase shows up here, in Orders.

40
00:02:03,004 --> 00:02:05,997
Order forms are best when
you're selling online.

41
00:02:05,997 --> 00:02:10,051
They support order bumps, like
adding the smile plan at checkout,

42
00:02:10,051 --> 00:02:12,296
and one-click upsells after payment.

43
00:02:12,296 --> 00:02:16,225
Here, Ava bought whitening, and
added the smile plan as a bump.

44
00:02:17,075 --> 00:02:20,884
Wherever the money comes from,
it all lands in Transactions.

45
00:02:20,884 --> 00:02:25,835
The source column tells you whether each
payment came from an invoice, a link,

46
00:02:25,835 --> 00:02:28,565
Text2Pay, a subscription,
or an order form.

47
00:02:29,415 --> 00:02:30,466
Here's a pro tip.

48
00:02:30,466 --> 00:02:35,044
Use a payment link for anything you
sell again and again at a fixed price.

49
00:02:35,044 --> 00:02:38,013
Use Text2Pay for a one-off
amount to one person.

50
00:02:38,013 --> 00:02:43,085
And use an order form when you're selling
on your website, so you can add upsells.

51
00:02:43,941 --> 00:02:46,586
Now you have three fast ways to get paid.

52
00:02:46,586 --> 00:02:50,650
In the final lesson of this
module, we'll manage subscriptions,

53
00:02:50,650 --> 00:02:52,457
failed payments and refunds.

54
00:02:52,457 --> 00:02:53,360
See you there!
